        "original_id": "c72ca5fd-840b-5c59-8669-df6e4394c5ab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Baltimore's Marching Ravens, Baltimore Ravens\n- Places: M&T Bank Stadium, Owings Mills, Baltimore, Indianapolis\n- Products: The Band That Wouldn't Die\n- Topics: American football, NFL franchise relocation\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1947, Baltimore's Marching Ravens has supported three separate American football franchises.\n- In 1984, the NFL's Baltimore Colts franchise relocated controversially from Baltimore to Indianapolis, and Baltimore's Marching Ravens witnessed the move.\n- Baltimore's Marching Ravens is the official marching band of the Baltimore Ravens American football team.\n- The Band That Wouldn't Die follows the story of Baltimore's Marching Ravens.\n- The Baltimore Ravens play their home games at M&T Bank Stadium.\n- The Baltimore Ravens are headquartered in Owings Mills.",
